<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <parent>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
        <version>3.4.1</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <groupId>com.moneyreserve</groupId>
    <artifactId>moneyreserve-api</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <name>moneyreserve-api</name>
    <description>MoneyReserve API — sign-in, SMS-derived spending insights, categorisation and budgets</description>

    <properties>
        <java.version>21</java.version>
        <springdoc.version>2.7.0</springdoc.version>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <!-- App sign-in: JWT signing and validation (Nimbus, version managed by Spring Boot). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-security-oauth2-jose</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
            <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
            <version>${springdoc.version}</version>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.h2database</groupId>
            <artifactId>h2</artifactId>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Flyway (DB migrations). Spring Boot 3.4 / Flyway 10 needs the
             PostgreSQL module as a separate dependency. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
            <optional>true</optional>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-security-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <excludes>
                        <exclude>
                            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                        </exclude>
                    </excludes>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <annotationProcessorPaths>
                        <path>
                            <groupId>org.projectlombok</groupId>
                            <artifactId>lombok</artifactId>
                        </path>
                    </annotationProcessorPaths>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                Integration tests (DIP section 30).

                Naming convention: *IT.java is an integration test and runs under Failsafe at
                the `verify` phase; everything else is a unit test and runs under Surefire at
                `test`. Surefire's default includes are Test*/*Test/*Tests/*TestCase, so the two
                sets cannot overlap and no test is ever run twice.

                verify is bound explicitly. Without it Failsafe runs the tests, writes its
                reports and never fails the build: a configuration that technically runs and
                checks nothing, which is worse than no integration tests at all because it looks
                like coverage on a report.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                <configuration>
                    <includes>
                        <include>**/*IT.java</include>
                    </includes>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>integration-tests</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>integration-test</goal>
                            <goal>verify</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!--
                JaCoCo. Report-only for now, on purpose.
                A coverage threshold set before anyone has seen a number is a number somebody
                invented; this run produces the baseline, and the check goal with a real minimum
                follows once that baseline is known. Both agents are attached because unit and
                integration tests cover different code, and merging them is the only way the
                figure describes the service rather than one half of its test suite.
            -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
                <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>unit-agent</id>
                        <goals><goal>prepare-agent</goal></goals>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>integration-agent</id>
                        <goals><goal>prepare-agent-integration</goal></goals>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>merge-exec</id>
                        <phase>post-integration-test</phase>
                        <goals><goal>merge</goal></goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <fileSets>
                                <fileSet>
                                    <directory>${project.build.directory}</directory>
                                    <includes>
                                        <include>jacoco.exec</include>
                                        <include>jacoco-it.exec</include>
                                    </includes>
                                </fileSet>
                            </fileSets>
                            <destFile>${project.build.directory}/jacoco-merged.exec</destFile>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>merged-report</id>
                        <phase>verify</phase>
                        <goals><goal>report</goal></goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <dataFile>${project.build.directory}/jacoco-merged.exec</dataFile>
                            <outputDirectory>${project.build.directory}/site/jacoco-merged</outputDirectory>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

    <profiles>
        <!--
            Dependency vulnerability scan.

            In a profile, activated by the presence of NVD_API_KEY, rather than bound
            unconditionally. Without a key the NVD feed is rate-limited hard enough that the first
            build takes hours or times out, and a gate that makes every developer build unusable
            gets disabled within a week, which leaves the project with no scan at all and a plugin
            in the pom that says otherwise.

            With the key present it runs on every `verify` and FAILS the build at CVSS 7.0 or
            above. Request a key at https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key and put it
            in CI's environment; do not commit it.
        -->
        <profile>
            <id>security-scan</id>
            <activation>
                <property>
                    <name>env.NVD_API_KEY</name>
                </property>
            </activation>
            <build>
                <plugins>
                    <plugin>
                        <groupId>org.owasp</groupId>
                        <artifactId>dependency-check-maven</artifactId>
                        <version>10.0.4</version>
                        <configuration>
                            <nvdApiKey>${env.NVD_API_KEY}</nvdApiKey>
                            <failBuildOnCVSS>7</failBuildOnCVSS>
                            <formats>
                                <format>HTML</format>
                                <format>JSON</format>
                            </formats>
                            <!-- No suppression file. A finding suppressed before anyone has
                                 read it is a finding nobody will ever read. -->
                        </configuration>
                        <executions>
                            <execution>
                                <phase>verify</phase>
                                <goals><goal>check</goal></goals>
                            </execution>
                        </executions>
                    </plugin>
                </plugins>
            </build>
        </profile>
    </profiles>
</project>
